  "overview": "**Talend Design System** is a light-first design system anchored on `hsla(0, 0%, 97%, 1)` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (18.4:1 contrast) and `hsla(204, 96%, 18%, 1)` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `Source Sans Pro` (16px display down to 16px body), unified by `0.25rem` base corner radius and subtle shadow elevation.\n\nMaintained by **Talend**. Source: published token package (https://github.com/Talend/ui/tree/master/packages/design-tokens#readme), package `@talend/design-tokens`. Inventory: **91** colors, **2** typography steps, and **18** documented components (Apache-2.0 license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 18 component tokens with documented paddings: `2.25rem`, `0 0 0 0.5rem`, `0`, `0.5rem`, `0 0.5rem`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `hsla(0, 0%, 97%, 1)` cards; separate sibling sections using `hsla(0, 0%, 65%, 1)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Layered Shadow Model**: Uses documented shadows (`0 0.125rem 0.375rem 0 hsla(0, 0%, 0%, 0.3)`, `0 0.125rem 0.375rem 0 hsla(0, 0%, 0%, 0.3)`) paired with `hsla(0, 0%, 65%, 1)` borders for elevated overlays.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `hsla(204, 96%, 18%, 1)` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `hsla(0, 0%, 97%, 1)` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `hsla(204, 96%, 18%, 1)` with `#f7f7f8` text (11.6:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Source Sans Pro` headings with `Source Sans Pro` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `0.25rem` base geometry across inputs and buttons (0.5rem on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `hsla(0, 0%, 97%, 1)` surface shifts and `hsla(0, 0%, 65%, 1)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `0.25rem` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `Input-module` fields and secondary buttons."
}
